Rationale: The claim states that 'the Redemptress' was the nickname of the orphaned Brazilian heiress who signed the Lei Aurea. While evidence confirms that Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, signed the Lei Aurea, there is no reliable evidence that Isabel was an orphaned heiress or that she was known by the nickname 'the Redemptress'. These material parts of the claim remain insufficiently supported and are not established by the provided evidence.
